{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1116270-rank-and-experience-question","id":1116270,"title":"Rank and experience question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-14T23:41:34-07:00","id":1116270,"title":"Rank and experience question","content":"Just a quick question to settle an argument. When a garou achieves a new rank, does his experience zero out and start at zero again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12334-chemscout","name":"Chemscout","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T23:49:54-07:00","id":1116274,"title":"","content":"Nope, I don't see why it would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T02:14:59-07:00","id":1116301,"title":"","content":"Sorry, that should have been &quot;Renown&quot; not experience. I apologize for the error. When a garou rises in rank, does his new zero out and start fresh with that rank?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12334-chemscout","name":"Chemscout","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T06:54:14-07:00","id":1116360,"title":"","content":"When the temporary renown gets converted into a permanent dot yes, the temp track goes to zero. However if you have enough permanent renown to go to the next rank the temp doesn't get reset","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 07-15-2017, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T03:34:46-07:00","id":1119446,"title":"","content":"I don't exactly know what the official rule books say, but my storyteller says that advancing in rank resets renown to the baseline requirements for the rank. For example, in W20, when a ragabash character rises from rank 1 to rank 2, he starts at rank 2 with exactly 7 permanent renown dots, even if he had 8 or more permanent renown before passing the test. I didn't like that at first, but he explained that this would keep a character from advancing too quickly from rank 1 to rank 3 if he became over-qualified in renown before passing the test for rank 2. I feel this is something the storyteller should feel okay tweaking according to what seems best for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T12:59:27-07:00","id":1119610,"title":"","content":"Your ST is using a house rule. It is explicitly not how the RAW work.<br /> <br /> Also, even if you have 10 permanent Renown in each category, you don't gain Rank until you undergo a Rank Challenge. If you're gaining Renown very rapidly, it doesn't mean you have the stats to win your Rank Challenges easily (and the higher the Rank, the challenges are supposed to be hard enough that the success rate is low on top of it). Temporary Renown doesn't go above 10, and doesn't automatically turn over to permanent; it takes a Rite or a few unique circumstances. Gaining 20 temporary Renown before your Rite of Accomplishment, you get one permanent Renown out of it.<br /> <br /> Now, there's lots of good reasons to adjust the Renown system (because you can still move incredibly fast despite everything I said above), but it's a lot easier to do so by reducing temporary Renown gains (esp. in scale with Rank). Removing permanent Renown gains to slow PC progression down is a dick ST move to me. If you don't want Renown gains to happen that fast, don't give out that much Renown.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T21:09:55-07:00","id":1119761,"title":"","content":"\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1116270-rank-and-experience-question?p=1119610#post1119610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your ST is using a house rule. It is explicitly not how the RAW work.<br /> <br /> Also, even if you have 10 permanent Renown in each category, you don't gain Rank until you undergo a Rank Challenge. If you're gaining Renown very rapidly, it doesn't mean you have the stats to win your Rank Challenges easily (and the higher the Rank, the challenges are supposed to be hard enough that the success rate is low on top of it). Temporary Renown doesn't go above 10, and doesn't automatically turn over to permanent; it takes a Rite or a few unique circumstances. Gaining 20 temporary Renown before your Rite of Accomplishment, you get one permanent Renown out of it.<br /> <br /> Now, there's lots of good reasons to adjust the Renown system (because you can still move incredibly fast despite everything I said above), but it's a lot easier to do so by reducing temporary Renown gains (esp. in scale with Rank). Removing permanent Renown gains to slow PC progression down is a dick ST move to me. If you don't want Renown gains to happen that fast, don't give out that much Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I realize all that, and my game's storyteller understands that rewarding renown should scale to reflect the character's rank. I believe that's actually part of his reasoning for &quot;resetting&quot; a character's permanent renown dots to the baseline for the new rank after the rank challenge is successfully passed. His argument is that the character shouldn't keep the extra permanent renown as though it were earned at the higher rank. On the other hand, he also isn't requiring us to ask for a rite of accomplishment to convert 10 temporary dots into a permanent dot, and at a difficulty of 4 for the rite, I'm okay with not role-playing that, and trusting him to reward the characters with appropriate renown in the first place. The chance of having permanent dots reduced after advancing in rank does sounds a bit kludgy as a hedge against characters rising too fast, but he is definitely not one to make &quot;dick ST moves.&quot; I just thought it might be helpful to share his idea since the topic came up, and as far as I've read, the question is not addressed in the W20 core book, though if you can point me to where, or to the right W20 book, please do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T03:14:58-07:00","id":1119820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1116270-rank-and-experience-question?p=1119761#post1119761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200bHis argument is that the character shouldn't keep the extra permanent renown as though it were earned at the higher rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really doesn't make any sense. A lower Ranked werewolf that earns a bunch of permanent Renown is more impressive, because they have less stuff to do it with. It's called Renown for a reason. It's a measure of your character's fame based on their deeds. A Cliath Ahroun that amasses a bunch of permanent Glory from killing a bunch of the Wyrm's minions in a relatively short amount of time has made a name for themselves as a prodigy of combat. That doesn't disappear because they become a Fostern, and it certainly doesn't become less impressive just because a Fostern Ahroun wouldn't be a renowned for the same actions (since a Fostern is expected to be better and such).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just thought it might be helpful to share his idea since the topic came up, and as far as I've read, the question is not addressed in the W20 core book, though if you can point me to where, or to the right W20 book, please do. </div> </div> </div>It's &quot;not addressed&quot; in the same way W20 doesn't address how to resolve rolling a natural 20 on your attack roll. It never says to do this, just like it never says to use d20s when rolling, which is all the addressing the topic needs.<br /> <br /> The Renown section (the part the defines Renown in general, not the chart of Renown awards) points out that Permanent Renown rarely changes, and generally only does so during the Rite of Accomplishment to go up, or Punishment Rites to go down. If Rank was supposed to change it, it would say so there, because it would really matter there.<br /> <br /> In the section on gaining Rank, it never says to modify a characters Renown at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}